.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library parses 5BSD application bundles (.app directories) and provides
access to their service declarations, metadata, and executables.
.Pp
A bundle has the structure:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Name.app/
  Contents/
    5BSD/
      Services/
        service.ucl     (one or more UCL service files)
    bin/
      program           (executables referenced by service UCL)
    Resources/          (optional application data)
.Ed
.Pp
Each Service.ucl file declares both bundle metadata
.Pq bundle_id, version, author
and a service definition
.Pq program, provides, requires, capabilities .
A bundle may contain up to 32 services.
.Ss Bundle Lifecycle
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Fn appbundle_open
parses the bundle directory and all Service.ucl files.
.It
.Fn appbundle_verify
validates integrity: binaries exist, provides are unique, no self-cycles.
.It
.Fn appbundle_svc_fill_manifest
converts a parsed service to a
.Vt struct svc_manifest
for use by
.Xr serviced 8 .
.It
.Fn appbundle_close
frees all resources.
.El
.Ss Service.ucl Format
Each Service.ucl file is a UCL document with the following keys:
.Bl -tag -width "capabilities"
.It Va bundle_id
(string, required for verification)
Reverse-domain bundle identifier.
Maximum 128 characters.
.It Va version
(string, optional)
Version string.
Maximum 32 characters.
.It Va author
(string, optional)
Author name.
Maximum 128 characters.
.It Va program
(string, required)
Executable name relative to
.Pa Contents/bin/ .
.It Va provides
(string or array, required for verification)
One or more service names this service provides for the dependency graph.
Maximum 8 entries; names must fit serviced's manifest label limit.
.It Va requires
(string or array, optional)
Service names this service depends on.
Maximum 8 entries.
.It Va on_demand
(boolean, optional)
If true, the service is launched on first lookup rather than at boot.
Default: false.
.It Va restart
(string, optional)
Restart policy:
.Dq always ,
.Dq on-failure ,
or
.Dq never .
Default:
.Dq never .
Unknown values produce a syslog warning and default to never.
.It Va stop_timeout
(integer, optional)
Seconds to wait for graceful shutdown before SIGKILL.
Clamped to range 1\(en300.
Default: 5.
.It Va max_failures
(integer, optional)
Consecutive rapid restarts before disabling service.
Clamped to range 1\(en100.
Default: 10.
.It Va user
(string, optional)
Username for privilege drop.
Maximum 64 characters.
.It Va group
(string, optional)
Group name for privilege drop.
Maximum 64 characters.
.It Va capabilities
(object, optional)
Capability claims to delegate to the service.
See
.Sx CAPABILITIES
below.
.El
.Ss CAPABILITIES
The
.Va capabilities
object may contain the following sub-keys:
.Bl -tag -width "network"
.It Va system
Array of system gate name strings.
These correspond to kernel-level operation gates defined in
.In dev/cap_rt/cap_rt_system_proto.h .
Valid gate names:
.Dq kldload ,
.Dq kldunload ,
.Dq kldstat ,
.Dq reboot ,
.Dq swapon ,
.Dq swapoff ,
.Dq sysctl ,
.Dq kenv ,
.Dq kenv_read ,
.Dq acct ,
.Dq audit .
Unknown names produce a syslog warning and are ignored.
.It Va paths
Array of absolute filesystem paths (strings).
Maximum 16 entries.
Non-absolute paths produce a warning and are skipped.
.It Va files
Array of file capability objects, each with:
.Bl -tag -width "actions" -compact
.It Va path
(required) Absolute filesystem path.
.It Va actions
(optional) Action list: string, array, or
.Dq * .
Valid actions:
.Dq read ,
.Dq write ,
.Dq append ,
.Dq create ,
.Dq delete ,
.Dq stat ,
.Dq lookup ,
.Dq exec ,
.Dq rename_from ,
.Dq rename_to ,
.Dq link ,
.Dq setattr ,
.Dq truncate ,
.Dq connect .
Default if missing or
.Dq * :
all actions.
.El
Maximum 16 entries.
.It Va network
Array of network endpoint objects, each with:
.Bl -tag -width "direction" -compact
.It Va port
Integer port number, range string
.Pq e.g., Dq 80-8000 ,
.Dq *
for all, or
.Dq .<1024
for privileged ports.
Default: all ports (0\(en65535).
Port values exceeding 65535 are rejected.
.It Va ports
Alias for
.Va port .
.It Va protocol
.Dq tcp ,
.Dq udp ,
.Dq any ,
or
.Dq * .
Default: any.
.It Va direction
.Dq bind ,
.Dq connect ,
.Dq any ,
or
.Dq * .
Default: bind.
.It Va domain
.Dq inet ,
.Dq inet6 ,
.Dq any ,
or
.Dq * .
Default: inet.
.It Va address
IP address or CIDR notation
.Pq e.g., Dq 192.168.1.0/24 .
.It Va prefix
Explicit CIDR prefix length (0\(en32 for inet, 0\(en128 for inet6).
.El
Maximum 16 entries.
Invalid entries produce a warning and are skipped.
.It Va jails
Array of jail capability objects or shorthand values.
Each element may be:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
An integer (jail ID).
.It
A string (jail name, maximum 63 characters).
.It
An object with keys:
.Va jid
(integer),
.Va name
(string),
.Va actions
(string or array:
.Dq create ,
.Dq get ,
.Dq set ,
.Dq remove ,
.Dq attach ,
.Dq * ) .
.El
Maximum 16 entries.
Entries with neither jid nor name are skipped.
.El
.Ss Verification Checks
.Fn appbundle_verify
performs:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
bundle_id must be present in at least one Service.ucl.
.It
Each service's program binary must exist and be executable.
.It
Each service must provide at least one name.
.It
No duplicate provides within the bundle.
.It
No service may require its own provides.
.El
.Ss Cycle Detection
.Fn appbundle_check_cycles
uses Kahn's algorithm across all provided bundles to detect circular
dependencies in the provides/requires graph.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning int return 0 on success and \-1 on error.
When
.Fa errbuf
is non-NULL, a descriptive error message is written on failure
identifying the bundle name, the failing service, and the specific issue.
.Pp
.Fn appbundle_service ,
.Fn appbundle_svc_provides ,
.Fn appbundle_svc_requires ,
and
.Fn appbundle_svc_cap_path
return NULL if the index is out of bounds.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr serviced 8 ,
.Xr servicectl 8 ,
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr cap_rt_system 4
